 "captions": [
  [0.3,7.2,"It was already one in the morning; the rain pattered dismally against the panes, and my candle was nearly burnt out…","Mary Shelley, Frankenstein"],
  [11.3,16.8,"My dear Victor, do not waste your time upon this; it is sad trash.","Victor’s father, Frankenstein, Chapter 2"],
  [17.4,19.3,"I opened it with apathy…",""],
  [29.9,34.7,"If, instead of this remark, my father had taken the pains to explain to me…","Victor Frankenstein, Chapter 2"],
  [44.6,49.6,"A flash of lightning illuminated the object, and discovered its shape plainly to me…","Frankenstein, Chapter 7"],
  [52.6,54.3,"…and some books.",""],
  [54.6,56.4,"Hold on. He can read?",""],
  [56.7,63.0,"He taught himself. He’s spent months hiding next to a cottage, listening to a family through a gap in the wall.",""],
  [63.3,64.3,"Go on.",""],
  [64.6,72.2,"I can hardly describe to you the effect of these books. They produced in me an infinity of new images and feelings…","Frankenstein, Chapter 15"]
